<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40753" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-dōno</span></b> , āvi,
			1, v. a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to give back again</i>, <i>restore</i>, <i>return</i> (only in Hor.).
			* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quis te redonavit dis patriis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 2, 7, 3</span></i>
			.— * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To give up</i>, <i>resign</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">graves Iras et invisum nepotem Marti redonabo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 3, 33</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
